<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marburg is a university town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahn">Lahn</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It grew around a castle of the landgraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> and later of Hesse, and the Church of St Elizabeth, built over the tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-of-hungary">Elizabeth of Hungary</a>, made it a pilgrimage centre. Philip I of Hesse founded its university in 1527, and from 1567 to 1604 it was the seat of the Landgraviate of Hesse-Marburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marburg.jpg" alt="Marburg" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PhilippN · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marburg_Schloss.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
